{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts","id":1543006,"title":"The Isle of Splintered Dreams thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-02T09:45:50-07:00","id":1543006,"title":"The Isle of Splintered Dreams thoughts","content":"So a new adventure was published free on Renegade's site.<br /> <br /> Some initial thoughts;<br /> <br /> I haven't gone through the adventure part yet, but the NPCs and the caern don't look too good.<br /> <br /> The caern is written not as a WtA caern but as the rock pile of real world.<br /> <br /> The NPC rival pack is frankly insulting. Even for a free adventure, I'd still wish the characters written would be werewolves and not humans.<br /> <br /> We have three Silver Fangs, a Raggie Influencer who does not care for the Litany. A Theurge trustfund baby that is as deep as that. An ahroun former football player who loves the former two ladies.<br /> <br /> We have the Ahroun's football buddy who is a Red Talon Ahroun with a football-caused headtrauma. He is highly implied to be mentally handicapped.<br /> <br /> A Glass Walker Raggie who simps the Fang raggie and goes by the name of Puppy-Boy.<br /> <br /> A Bone Gnawer Galliard who... likes to sneak and stay hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T10:15:45-07:00","id":1543010,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that we can probably assume at this point that W5 isn't going to experience the miracles of revision that SR6 did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T11:17:07-07:00","id":1543017,"title":"","content":"What the fuck is going on with that cover art?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T11:24:12-07:00","id":1543019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543017#post1543017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the fuck is going on with that cover art?</div> </div> </div> </div>Photobashing until the artist realised they had to actually DRAW a wolf XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T11:58:30-07:00","id":1543022,"title":"","content":"I will write a review tomorrow when I have more time but I just read the Introduction and I'm already at the point of &quot;Wait, what?!&quot;.<ul><li>The setting is &quot;any caern on an island&quot; but (of course) the assumed setting is the Great Lakes in the US. God forbid, anything in W5 doesn't center North America or Europe...</li> <li>The description of the island is just a mess.</li> <li>You have a rival-Pack of Garou which are bad when their general aim is to spurn Garou tradition. So Garou traditions are good now, I guess...</li> <li>Also the way in which this rival-Pack spurns tradition seems more like a parody of that idea. The main-part is that this bad Garou Pack is led by a trio of &quot;spoiled rich kids&quot;... We're talking about Garou and the characterization is just &quot;spoiled rich kids&quot;.</li> <li>The leader of the eco-activists in the area is a Fomor and has been taken over by a Bane-Spirit which means they're a bad-guy-faction.</li> <li>The goons of the logging-company are really just bystanders. Their aims are bad (they're a greedy logging-company) but they're just innocent mortals at the end of the day.</li> <li>The Introduction claims the point of this adventure is to keep the players guessing who the real threat is... Nothing of this is subversive or clever. Okay, the eco-activist leader is the Fomor this time around... Okay, so you kill him instead this time around. But once you remove the switcheroo on that count, it's the same-old formula again. Of course, the logging-company is bad! That is just a really hamfisted attempt at trying to be clever.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T12:48:42-07:00","id":1543025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543022#post1543022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>You have a rival-Pack of Garou which are bad when their general aim is to spurn Garou tradition. So Garou traditions are good now, I guess...</li> <li>Also the way in which this rival-Pack spurns tradition seems more like a parody of that idea. The main-part is that this bad Garou Pack is led by a trio of &quot;spoiled rich kids&quot;... We're talking about Garou and the characterization is just &quot;spoiled rich kids&quot;.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it is nice they switch it up a bit that SOME rivals are irrelevant about tradition and some are loyal to it.<br /> <br /> But these characters are just humans. You could change them into a hunter group or a vampire coterie and nothing would need to be changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T13:12:42-07:00","id":1543026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543025#post1543025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it is nice they switch it up a bit that SOME rivals are irrelevant about tradition and some are loyal to it.<br /> <br /> But these characters are just humans. You could change them into a hunter group or a vampire coterie and nothing would need to be changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and they simply aren't interesting. They were clearly written with the intent to be &quot;bad Garou&quot; - except what makes them bad has nothing to do with them being Garou like you mentioned. It feels like this adventure expects the PCs to just lecture these characters for being bad. Even in the Introduction, you get stuff like &quot;or is it possible to force their rivals to take the responsibility seriously?&quot;. I would be really interested in asking the writer why they chose &quot;force&quot; there but aside from that, it's clear what this adventure thinks of them.<br /> <br /> The point of the adventure is to present a complicated situation and see where PCs think they see the true evil but instead you just get presented with annoyances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T16:40:27-07:00","id":1543036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543022#post1543022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will write a review tomorrow when I have more time but I just read the Introduction and I'm already at the point of &quot;Wait, what?!&quot;.<ul><li>The setting is &quot;any caern on an island&quot; but (of course) the assumed setting is the Great Lakes in the US. God forbid, anything in W5 doesn't center North America or Europe...</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Again I just have to say that WtE also limits they setting to north west US though they make it clear that it's so they can more easily research the native culture of the area...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543022#post1543022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will write a review tomorrow when I have more time but I just read the Introduction and I'm already at the point of &quot;Wait, what?!&quot;.<ul><li>You have a rival-Pack of Garou which are bad when their general aim is to spurn Garou tradition. So Garou traditions are good now, I guess...</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually now that I think about it having the PCs teach a wayward pack of Garou about they traditions could be a interesting premise for a adventure. Like all the other stuff in the adventure is just background nose the main focuse should be about the players mentoring the pack on how to be true warriors of Gaia. Hell to make things even funner make it clear they got all they knowledge about the garou from W5 which in universe is a Pentex product...<br /> <br /> Edit: Also swap out the pack for something less shallow or at very least re write them to give a bit more deph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 10-02-2024, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T17:04:40-07:00","id":1543037,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen any art yet but the NPCs all seem very WASPy from their descriptions...not that that's unusual for W5 releases so far...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T20:35:45-07:00","id":1543045,"title":"","content":"I can see what the intent is for the adventure - the antagonists aren't actually bad (except for the fomor) and the players have to try and navigate that. But the actual implementation looks like a mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T23:31:41-07:00","id":1543088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543045#post1543045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see what the intent is for the adventure - the antagonists aren't actually bad (except for the fomor) and the players have to try and navigate that. But the actual implementation looks like a mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll say it again it should have been about the players actually mentoring the rouge pack while the other stuff would be set dressing or maybe learnable moments for the pack. Although that would nauseate the rouge pack not being walking seterotypes and have a bit more depth to enable character development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T06:36:17-07:00","id":1543095,"title":"","content":"Some more thoughts:<ul><li>Having read the whole thing now, I can't help but get a whole &quot;rushed first draft&quot;-vibe from this adventure. There's so much here that feels half-baked.</li> <li>All of the Garou-characters seem way too human.</li> <li>The adventure also plays fast and loose with the systems and mechanics it introduces. And I'm pretty sure you will run into trouble if you run this exactly as it's described.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Characters</span><br /> <br /> Mother Ida:<ul><li>First off, get a taste of this tortured sentence in the Introduction: &quot;The caern is protected by a sept that is really only a pack of one \u2014 Mother Ida, a Garou who is long in the tooth.&quot; Of course, it's clear what the writing is getting at. She's the last surviving member of the guarding Pack. But... one Pack is not a Sept and one Garou isn't a Pack.</li> <li>Also, what's weird about her character is that one important character in the Scent of Decay supplement was Mother Louise... who's also an older Children of Gaia Theurge. It's pretty much the same character except in Scent of Decay the character was black and here she's white.</li> <li>And you get a taste of her way too human characterization in this bit: : &quot;However, it\u2019s possible for the players\u2019 pack to ease her life enough that she may find the strength for a few more years. A successful Wits + Medicine test at a Difficulty of 3 allows a character to notice that replacing her cheap off-the-shelf reading glasses with better ones or getting her a hearing aid would make her life easier.&quot; You\u2019re telling me this Garou Elder needs better reading glasses and a hearing-aid and if she doesn\u2019t have that, she will die a few years earlier\u2026? Come on!</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Face of Gaia Pack</span><ul><li>You got six members and a trio of Silver Fangs leads them. That trio is called &quot;The Silver Smile Throuple&quot;. Not only are these three Silver Fangs who are spoiled rich kids but they're also in a messy sexual relationship with each other. The absurdity only intensifies when you get to the individual characters as well...</li> <li>The role of them as &quot;bad Garou&quot; feels forced. There's a sidebar on pg 18 that explains the two main-issues. The first one is that they're thrill-seeking glory-hounds. It's also suggested that the three Silver Fangs already suffer from Hauglosk... And that gets to the second issue which is that the Pack isn't interested in guarding the caern long-term. And the sidebar ends with &quot;If pressed on this second issue, they know the caern is going to fall if left unguarded but they try to justify their choices by saying that the Apocalypse is here anyway so long-term commitment is meaningless.\u200b&quot;</li> <li>But with that setup, isn't the solution pretty obvious? Unless you want this Pack to be comically evil, selfish and inept, the obvious compromise here is to let this Pack fight the Fomor (maybe with some assistance from the PC Pack), get the Renown for that and then you just let them move on while the PC Pack becomes the new guardians of the caern. If they have no interest in becoming guardians of the caern, why would they be interested in stopping the Rite that would make the PC Pack the new guardians...?</li> </ul><br /> Face of Gaia Pack-members:<ul><li>Diamond-Eyes/Jewels Devore (Silver Fang Ragabash): She's pretty much an egotistical social media influencer interested in becoming famous. And it says &quot;The young Silver Fang is always trying to push boundaries and even reject traditional Garou teachings. She cares little about things like the Litany and goes to any length to please her adoring online fans.\u200b&quot; But if that's true, why is she the leader of a Pack that's all about earning Renown...?</li> <li>Shadow-Mane/Dita Arya (Silver Fang Theurge): The descriptions previously say that these three lead as a trio but with both this description and the next one, it's made clear that Diamond Eyes is the one true leader. It says &quot;She is a trust-fund diva Silver Fang, more a follower than a leader. She is always looking for others to make decisions as long as those decisions include her and don\u2019t call for her to put in much effort \u2014 unless it\u2019s paying for something or talking to spirits.\u200b</li> <li>Tall-Walker/Cash Wagner (Silver Fang Ahroun): It can all be boiled down to this: &quot;A former collegiate three-sport athlete, this sculpted Adonis carries himself with an air of authority and thinks of himself as a tough guy and enforcer. In all truth, he is not too smart, insanely jealous, and fairly dangerous.\u200b&quot; Okay, so it's an Ahroun who's strong but stupid. Not very inspired choice.</li> <li>Crazy-Claw/Cody Carver (Red Talon Ahroun): It can all be boiled down to this: &quot;He is a frat brother, a football teammate, and a loyal best friend to Cash. Crazy-Claw solves all problems with violence and can follow only the simplest strategies.\u200b&quot; Okay, so it's an Ahroun who's strong but... Hang on a second! I wrote this already! Yeah, this Pack has two Ahroun that are pretty much the same character! That's what I mean by this having a &quot;first-draft-vibe&quot;. You already had a pretty basic Ahroun-character-concept here but then this book goes ahead and puts two versions of that same concept in the book.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Rite of the Blood Warden</span><ul><li>In the second half of the adventure you fight the Fomor and you fight the Face of Gaia Pack but it's also about this Rite that allows Mother Ida to change responsibility from Mother Ida to the PC Pack.</li> <li>Part of the Rite is that you need eight (!) specific ingredients. Some Mother Ida already has but the others are pretty much turned into fetch-quests by this adventure.</li> <li>And some of the ingredients are so specific that I have a hard time believing that every player-group will know where to look for these.</li> <li>Some examples: &quot;A consecrated Boline, a specific type of a ritual knife (Good luck, but you can likely find a silver knife in Longlook).\u200b&quot; (Why would the PCs think that you can find something like that in a small town with 200 people...?)</li> <li>&quot;An offering bowl made from local clay (there is some local pottery in Longlook).\u200b&quot; (Again, how are PCs supposed to know that...?!)</li> <li>Or &quot;Hair from a child born in summer, who died in autumn (find someone born during summer month and it is currently autumn, all they need to do is die; or you could look for a graveyard and get lucky).\u200b&quot; (And what does the &quot;get lucky&quot;-phrase here mean anyway...? Obviously, if the players simply can't find this ingredient for whatever reason, it would bring the adventure to a screeching halt! Why would you write something like that into your adventure...?)</li> <li>The write-up for the Rite also makes little sense: &quot;The Difficulty to perform this Rite is 2 plus 1 for each new guardian beyond the first.\u200b&quot; And normally Mother Ida would perform the Rite with everybody with at least one dot in Occult adding a die who joins the Rite (not a Rage-die like the corebook suggests for some reason). Mother Ida has a dicepool of 7. So, say you have four PCs and let's say all have at least one dot in Occult. That would mean this book suggests you roll 11 dice for a Difficulty 6 test. Hey, good luck with that...</li> <li>But what really takes the cake is the confrontation with the Face of Gaia Pack. Unless any members of the enemy Pack are taken out, all six are there. And here comes the kicker: &quot;Each part of the Rite takes 1 round \u2014 Place the bowl, Hand, Hair, Heart, and current guardian\u2019s Blood, 1 round\u200b each per new guardian\u2019s Blood, catch on fire, turn to ash (Minimum 8 rounds +1 round per new guardian beyond the first). Mother Ida and anyone helping her must be defended for at least 8 rounds to complete the Rite.\u200b&quot; The default for W5 is doing the &quot;three rounds and you're done&quot;-thing. With the four PC example, from above, this suggests this fight should last <i>at least</i> 12 rounds!</li> <li>And it says &quot;Only Tall-Walker and Crazy-Claw are warriors, and the two of them are more brawlers than tacticians.\u200b&quot;. It's like the writer completely forgot that these aren't just mundane humans they were writing about. All six of them can shift into their Crinos-Form!</li> <li>And here's the Storyteller-Advice in the book: &quot;For this, don\u2019t hold back. This is what the story has built up to and the players deserve an exciting and furious crescendo for their story. If things seem to be going too much the players\u2019 way, you could extend the time the Rite takes because Mother Ida fumbles at putting gifts into the offering bowl, or the strain might be too much for her and she might need to stop to catch her breath \u2014 giving more time for the Rite to be interrupted. Now don\u2019t cheat the players out of victory, but make them feel the tension so it\u2019s a story to remember.\u200b&quot; What can you even say here... There's no way this was playtested. Here, the writing is worrying about things going too well for the players. If anything, I would imagine the opposite of that will happen. The only way I could see this work is if you also have six players at your table. Then at least, it's somewhat balanced.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T06:54:08-07:00","id":1543096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543095#post1543095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some more thoughts:<ul><li>But with that setup, isn't the solution pretty obvious? Unless you want this Pack to be comically evil, selfish and inept, the obvious compromise here is to let this Pack fight the Fomor (maybe with some assistance from the PC Pack), get the Renown for that and then you just let them move on while the PC Pack becomes the new guardians of the caern. If they have no interest in becoming guardians of the caern, why would they be interested in stopping the Rite that would make the PC Pack the new guardians...?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Or ya know just have the players mentor the pack and set them straight. I mean yeah the St is gonna have to give them more character traits than frat stereotypes or even just replace all of them but it seems they gonna rework the adventure regardless, so why not just pivot to a more intresting aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T07:24:04-07:00","id":1543098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543096#post1543096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or ya know just have the players mentor the pack and set them straight. I mean yeah the St is gonna have to give them more character traits than frat stereotypes or even just replace all of them but it seems they gonna rework the adventure regardless, so why not just pivot to a more intresting aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that. It's also crucial to this adventure that the PC Pack wants to take over this caern. Because if for whatever reason, similar to the bad Garou Pack, they're not interested then this whole thing falls apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T07:45:12-07:00","id":1543099,"title":"","content":"In all fairness; This is a free adventure. High quality should not be expected.<br /> <br /> On the other, Gaia's Face pack suffers from the same issue most of the NPCs in Tribes of the Moon book for Forsaken did; The writer wrote humans and forgot to add the werewolf.<br /> <br /> Personally, should these characters even be werewolves? They could be a high school clique on vacation in the island and the PCs have to actually consider should they kill a bunch of kids or should they try to teach them a lesson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T08:17:53-07:00","id":1543102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543099#post1543099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, should these characters even be werewolves? They could be a high school clique on vacation in the island and the PCs have to actually consider should they kill a bunch of kids or should they try to teach them a lesson.</div> </div> </div> </div>or hell if you want to adapt it to the WtE setting just say they're a pack of freshly turned bitten that only stumbled across the remains of the cearen the player pack is scouting for they faction. They would have less than a week of experience of being a werewolf explaining why they act more like humans than wolves and the reason they might come to blows with the PC pack is because the only contact with a werewolf is the asshole who turned them and the only infomation they know about werewolves is a session of Lycanthrop: the Rapture 5e they played before being bitten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T09:13:21-07:00","id":1543104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543099#post1543099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all fairness; This is a free adventure. High quality should not be expected.<br /> <br /> On the other, Gaia's Face pack suffers from the same issue most of the NPCs in Tribes of the Moon book for Forsaken did; The writer wrote humans and forgot to add the werewolf.<br /> <br /> Personally, should these characters even be werewolves? They could be a high school clique on vacation in the island and the PCs have to actually consider should they kill a bunch of kids or should they try to teach them a lesson.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, high school clique sounds about right. The way they're written has some strong &quot;troubled teens&quot;-vibes.<br /> <br /> I think they could be one of those Gaian Cults that have been introduced in Shattered Nation. But not in the sense of them being an actual cult. You take the &quot;spoiled and rich&quot;-part away and you just make them young people who for whatever reason are somewhat aware of Gaia and the animistic truths of the world. And either due to them having some personal connection to Garou, having experienced Delirium personally in the past or being Kin, something has pushed them on this path where their goal is now to &quot;fight the Wyrm&quot; (or whatever this means to them).<br /> <br /> Also, I just had this idea: What if instead of Mother Ida being there, the Garou Pack gets there and this group of young people has looked at Mother Ida's notebook and they have performed the Rite. They are now the new guardians of this caern - except they're not Garou. Or if you go with the Kin-idea, they're not Garou yet. And now it's up to the PC Pack to help them with this responsibility. They want to be the guardians of this caern. And you play out what the players think of this. Do you help them and mentor them? Do you force them to switch guardianship to the PC Pack?<br /> <br /> Because I also think the adventure at the start says that this is supposed to be about keeping the players guessing what the real threat is but really, it's all obvious. According to the adventure, you have an actual Fomor and it's clear what needs to be done there. And the bad Garou Pack in the adventure attacks the PCs for wanting to be the next guardians. Also, they seem pretty bad. So in reality, there isn't a whole lot of guessing going on here. You really only start to introduce more uncertainty and guessing by having situations that aren't clear-cut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T11:30:14-07:00","id":1543113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543104#post1543104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I just had this idea: What if instead of Mother Ida being there, the Garou Pack gets there and this group of young people has looked at Mother Ida's notebook and they have performed the Rite. They are now the new guardians of this caern - except they're not Garou. Or if you go with the Kin-idea, they're not Garou yet. And now it's up to the PC Pack to help them with this responsibility. They want to be the guardians of this caern. And you play out what the players think of this. Do you help them and mentor them? Do you force them to switch guardianship to the PC Pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, THIS would be so cool. Not just because it uses the characters better, but ALSO because it showcases the nature of W5 much better. There are these regular humans in the Know who WANT to help and who are TRYING to help. But just aren't mature enough yet and just humans against supernatural forces.<br /> <br /> W5 has so much freedom in its setting and not seeing it being used is sad.<br /> <br /> Also, so far in W5, has there been one enviromental activist that has actually made an impact? XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T13:32:00-07:00","id":1543119,"title":"","content":"The NPCs in Red Tundra, Scent of Decay and What the Waters Hid aren't much better if at all.<br /> <br /> But then the NPCs in Shattered Nation feel mostly phoned in as well...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T03:08:49-07:00","id":1543193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543113#post1543113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, so far in W5, has there been one enviromental activist that has actually made an impact? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't understand what W5 expects Garou-PCs to do with this whole &quot;Garou are activists&quot;-idea. Because once again, the Fomor is this depressed/desperate eco-activist who under the influence of the Bane-Spirit convinced himself that violence is the only solution. And according to this adventure, this is bad and needs to be stopped. But then what does this game expect Garou-PC to do if you were to put them up against a completely mundane logging-company, for example?<br /> <br /> And the setup in this adventure leads to the PCs killing the leader of the eco-activists while doing absolutely nothing about the bad logging-company on the island. So that doesn't work exactly either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543119#post1543119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The NPCs in Red Tundra, Scent of Decay and What the Waters Hid aren't much better if at all.<br /> <br /> But then the NPCs in Shattered Nation feel mostly phoned in as well...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the character-writing ranges from mid to pretty terrible in these supplements.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T12:43:47-07:00","id":1543206,"title":"","content":"What Knightgale touches upon here touches upon something I\u2019ve heard a lot of other commentators point out about W5 and it\u2019s something I feel is a valuable point to make, albeit a difficult one in so far as it touches upon some highly sensitive and nuanced real world subjects. Namely the issue of political violence.<br /> <br /> WtA has always had the criticism of the Garou that they often were over-reliant upon violence and warfare as a means to achieving their ends (or, rather, not achieving their ends). The common refrain was that the Garou suffered because they were trying to fight industrial/post-industrial problems with Neolithic/Iron Age solutions. However this critique was largely about the failures of the Garou to make use of other necessary tactics and to attack the roots of the problem (\u2018attacking the root\u2019 meaning a need for radical solutions) rather then about the usefulness of violence as such - violence was useful and necessary but it could be harmful or ineffective if used improperly.<br /> <br /> The issue with W5 is one which is hard to describe succinctly but which I feel has elements of what I\u2019ll call either \u2018Historical Nihilism\u2019 or \u2018Liberal Nihilism\u2019 (Liberalism here not meaning liberal in the sense of Democrat v. Republican or Labour v. Tory but rather Liberalism in the sense of a post-1789 society governed by a bourgeois dictatorship with focus upon equality under the law, free trade/enterprise, the sanctity of private property, etc.). This school of Liberal Nihilism holds violence as a categorically illegitimate means of action and rejects radicalism (addressing the roots; the causes) in favor of reformism (addressing the fruits; the symptoms) at best. In its contemporary form it is heavily influenced by the historical nihilism of the post-1991 world which considers Liberalism the End of History, the Best of All Possible Worlds, and thus forecloses upon radical interventions of all stripes.<br /> <br /> The issue with this is that reformism is, I contend, fundamentally incapable of addressing existential crises to the system itself, crises which are not tangential to the foundational elements of the system but crises which derive from the foundational elements of the system itself, which can only be addressed by radical intervention, and which those who are most dependent on the system\u2019s continuation are least able to address. Werewolf has always made this clear by having as fundamental to its narrative the existential crises of ecology &amp; environmentalism (a somewhat flawed conception that can be addressed some other time), namely, that the Energy Regime of Modern Liberalism, dating back to the outbreak of the Industrial Revolution, is dependent upon Carbon Energy/Fossil Fuels (Coal, Oil, Gas, etc.). The continuation of global society as it currently exists is dependent upon the Regime of Oil and those most wedded to the Regime of Oil are the ones least able to address the ensuing crises. <br /> <br /> The limits of what is acceptable under Liberal Nihilism do not contain the means of addressing these root issues. Reformism, passive resistance, protest, electoralism, etc. would simply not be sufficient to win the War. However, to be fair to W5, neither would the purely adventurist campaigns of violence with the Garou have carried out from 1st edition to W20. Random assassinations, bombings, sabotage, &amp; guerrilla assaults are also not sufficient to win the War. Not even a dialectic combination of the two, imo, would be sufficient to win the war. The defeat of the Regime of Oil, if it does not come from the purely mechanical forces of history which will sweep away the old order with escalating disasters and crises, would require radical solutions. Solutions which not only address the roots of the Regime of Oil but also the current World Order (the order we have inherited from 1790, 1815, 1848, 1870, 1918, 1945, 1968, 1991, etc.).<br /> <br /> Earlier editions did not always perfectly address this imo either, although they may have come closer. There was already Historical Nihilism in WoD, especially imo, as time went on. However the acceptance of the possibility (and necessity) of radicalism which existed outside the bounds of Liberal Nihilism made those earlier editions closer to the mark than W5. <br /> <br /> Not everything has to be didactically written in such a fashion as to heighten revolutionary consciousness of course. Not every WtA adventure needs to include pages ripped from \u2018What Is To Be Done?\u2019, \u2018On Contradiction\u2019, or \u2018The Wretched of the Earth\u2019, but even from a purely narrative pov, setting aside real world considerations, imo the consideration of possibilities beyond the limits of Liberal Nihilism, especially for a gameline so rooted in the worlds before said Liberal Epoch, can only make the possibilities for storytelling and play alike more interesting and more engaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T14:00:48-07:00","id":1543212,"title":"","content":"Actually looking over the W5 scenarios released so far have we had more environmentalists being Fomor than anyone else? No..the Universal Brotherhoodesqe mob in SoD are just blue collar workers...still I think Boss Fomor have so far mostly been activists rather than capitalists or 1%ers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T05:41:42-07:00","id":1543856,"title":"","content":"The Gryffon15 post is a example for why I consider WtA the best rpg ever, I don't see any other rpg scenario given to us a lesson about Liberal Nihilism or End of History. Kudos, my friend","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T08:44:01-07:00","id":1543866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543206#post1543206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Isle of Splintered Dreams is a good showcase of this nihilism, I think. And the issue is more a W5 issue than a general WtA-issue because in W5 things have been pushed to &quot;The Garou Nation has fallen, it's the Age of Apocalypse and Gaia's dead/dying.&quot;.<br /> <br /> First, you got the Hauglosk-creed of W5. And here in this adventure you got the bad Garou Pack. On pg 18 you got a sidebar explaining their mindset and it ends with this: &quot;If pressed on this second issue, they know the caern is going to fall if left unguarded but they try to justify their choices by saying that the Apocalypse is here anyway so long-term commitment is meaningless.&quot; We've heard explanations like that before about Hauglosk and why it's bad. But I always thought it an appealing idea to play. And you're right in your explanation of this type of adventurism not fixing anything. But in the depressing setting of W5, the anger and self-righteousness of this outlook at least matches the dire state of the world. It's an anger that just asks &quot;When, if not the end-times...?&quot;. But it's nihilistic, of course. It won't change anything to go on this rampage. Gaia won't simply be resurrected because you've killed your thousandth Fomor.<br /> <br /> But there's a nihilism to what is outlined as the good scenario as well. The adventure describes that there has been a Garou-Pack guiding this caern since time immemorial. And now the last surviving member of the current Pack that guarded the caern calls out to the PC-Pack to take over. Presumably the good ending here is that the PC Pack do just that. They become the new guardians. But this changes nothing. There's always been a Garou Pack there and the world has gotten worse and worse around them. And what is the message of the supposed &quot;good ending&quot; where the PC Pack take over? Just keep on keeping on. It's the Age of Apocalypse and the good ending is &quot;Just do the same thing everybody else did before you. There's no need for change.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T15:08:51-07:00","id":1543915,"title":"","content":"Exactly. It\u2019s a good ending what\u2019s the best possible outcome we can imagine is the maintenance of the current status quo.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not against cynical stories in principle. It\u2019s certainly possible to tell a compelling story with a message that \u2018in conditions as dire as these, the only possible victory is just to survive another day\u2019. That can be done well and in a compelling fashion and it describes the experience of plenty of people in history and now. It can even be done well in a high power setting like werewolf where the exaggeration of Garou capabilities in comparison to an average person simply highlight the extremity of the struggle. There\u2019s nothing inherently wrong with that from a narrative level.<br /> <br /> It does however, imo, indicate the sort of \u2018Historical Nihilism\u2019 I described in my post above, which is valid to critique. It\u2019s nuanced but I think it\u2019s reasonable to make the distinction between those who live in such conditions which make survival itself a form of victory over the world and those who are consciously aware of the crises of the world but are personally in circumstances of such relative comfort that any possible change to the world order (except perhaps a form of reformism which grants them a greater share of the spoils of the current world order) can only represent an existential threat to their already precarious position. Such a position as described in the latter case, imo, can be soothing to the person who adopts it, by the notion that their resignation is merely a realistic analysis, rather then a self-interest excuse for moral cowardice.<br /> <br /> Of course, the thing about such \u2018moral cowardice\u2019 is that, it is typical for most people. Most people have some things they view as morally abhorrent and if they truly acted upon those convictions would be compelled to take some time of action against it. However, the majority of such persons, do not take any action which would seriously threaten their material position. The psychic anguish this produces can either be resolved into the acceptance of a state of false consciousness or be ameliorated in any number of ways but for many people, they will never truly overcome their \u2018moral cowardice\u2019. This statement is as much a confession as it is an accusation of others. <br /> <br /> That\u2019s one reason why, I believe, power fantasy narratives such as what Werewolf (or Batman, or Robin Hood, or what have you), are attractive. They allow one to vicariously act out through fictitious circumstances what it might look like to overcome this \u2018moral cowardice\u2019 though action of some type, action which crosses over the threshold which would produce consequences that would render one\u2019s relatively comfortable material circumstances impossible to persist. Werewolf has always worn this on its sleeve. The early storyteller advice sections, iirc, even encourage ones ST to make use of their own and their players angst to generate stories (ex: if you know a player at your table is a former fast food service employee, give them an opportunity to rip apart their shithead ex-manager in the form of an O\u2019Tooley\u2019s goon).<br /> <br /> Of course these power fantasies are not inherently virtuous. They do not inherently inspire those who participate in them towards right action (not every peasant small holder who loved Robin Hood stories would actually risk their own hide in attempting to cheat the manor lords or bishops out of their expected share of taxation and tithe, even if they may have wished to). To those who seek to produce right action in others this leads them either to condemn power-fantasy as \u2018an opiate of the masses\u2019 by another form or to qualify their support for the subject (for instance, the position that power fantasy can be useful, but it should be wedded with a program of political action, political education, etc.).<br /> <br /> In other cases, and I think Werewolf itself experienced this, even prior to W5, the power-fantasy is deemed a form of immaturity and is met with the vulgar-realism of the \u2018historical nihilist\u2019 who, whether more or less articulately, argues that a better world is not possible and that to attempt the radical assaults on the status quo that would be necessary to change it (and which would necessarily cause one to lose their position of relative security within the system) is misguided, immature, and irresponsible. <br /> <br /> To this point, it\u2019s not uncommon for valid critiques of irresponsible action (adventurism) to be conflated with all attempts at radical action. To Knightengale\u2019s above point, we can see this with the rival pack in this adventure. Adventurism actually exists and so it can certainly be represented and it\u2019s causes understood and expressed; but it can also be conflated with all forms of radical action, creating a false dichotomy between \u2018Perpetuate the Status Quo v. Attack the Status Quo in irresponsible &amp; ineffective ways for petty reasons\u2019. Of course, again, there\u2019s no reason one can\u2019t present a scenario where these are the primary perspectives represented, and there are cases where accurately representing the major active forces in a situation might require it, but imo, one can do this in such a way that is aware of the possibility of Right Action rather then one which posits only the false dichotomy described above. <br /> <br /> I hope that this has been clear and helpful for those interested in these sorts of metatextual discussions. I\u2019m afraid that parts of this may not be immediately clear to those not familiar with certain political mileaus lol so if anything here is unclear, please ask about it, and I\u2019ll try to clarify my points, to the best of my ability.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T00:15:40-07:00","id":1543957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543006-the-isle-of-splintered-dreams-thoughts?p=1543915#post1543915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To this point, it\u2019s not uncommon for valid critiques of irresponsible action (adventurism) to be conflated with all attempts at radical action. To Knightengale\u2019s above point, we can see this with the rival pack in this adventure. Adventurism actually exists and so it can certainly be represented and it\u2019s causes understood and expressed; but it can also be conflated with all forms of radical action, creating a false dichotomy between \u2018Perpetuate the Status Quo v. Attack the Status Quo in irresponsible &amp; ineffective ways for petty reasons\u2019..</div> </div> </div> </div>On the subject Status Quo vs change I would like to share this video:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Filg0MkpCrk?si=g8EQqgLhMo7a4zki\" data-code=\"Filg0MkpCrk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Filg0MkpCrk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Like the main subject of video Mlynar main character trait is being fervently opposed to any attempt to reform the current system of his country by his nieces. Some of his reasons for this attitude are rooted in legitimit concerns (mainly that the political interests that lead to the current situation is too entranced for mere activism to dislodge and they 're more than welling to resourt to force to take down any perceived threats) well others are more rooted in his emotions (His disillusionment on the concept of kinghood in general and his wish to have Neil name fade into history and not get tainted by associating with the event that reduces the once prestigious position of knights into glorified gladiators).<br /> <br /> Still unlike W5 where Mlynar's opposition to change seen as a &quot;regrettable necessity&quot; at very least in Arknights it's presented as genuine character flaw that he has to work to overcome. Culminating in him coming to the rescue of his nieces from government assassins. Implicitly supporting they cause for reform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}